{"chunk_id": "c29415eee9cd", "text": "King Janaka explains that many powerful kings once tried to string the sacred bow preserved by his dynasty, hoping to win Sita\u2019s hand, but none succeeded. Their humiliation even led to a year\u2011long siege of Mithila before Janaka defeated them. At Vishwamitra\u2019s request, the immense bow\u2014so heavy it must be brought on an eight\u2011wheeled cart by hundreds of men\u2014is presented to Rama. Calmly examining it, Rama lifts the divine weapon with ease and attempts to string it. In the act, his strength shatters the bow with a thunderous crack that shakes the earth and stuns the assembled crowd. Recognizing the miraculous feat, Janaka joyfully declares that his vow is fulfilled and promises Sita in marriage to Rama, sending messengers to invite King Dasaratha to witness the union.\nRama effortlessly lifts and breaks Shiva\u2019s bow before the assembly, proving his strength and winning King Janaka\u2019s promise of Sita\u2019s hand in marriage.\nThemes: divine strength, trial of worthiness, marriage alliance, destiny fulfilled", "vector": [-0.0062992568127810955, -0.0186337698251009, -0.0020318026654422283, 0.027322398498654366, -0.02021108940243721, 0.016749005764722824, -0.03274945169687271, -0.016347991302609444, -0.011067978106439114, -0.033391073346138, 0.004347656853497028, -0.0034821354784071445, 0.00759252579882741, 0.02959481067955494, 0.0016115737380459905, 0.017283689230680466, 0.04215990751981735, -0.021734941750764847, 0.023659806698560715, -0.030477039515972137, 0.007980172522366047, -0.028231363743543625, -0.007378651760518551, 0.016000445932149887, -0.02047843299806118, 0.003993427846580744, 0.014222619123756886, -0.033177200704813004, 0.02962154522538185, -0.01283243764191866, -0.009477290324866772, -0.0008262553019449115, -0.012438108213245869, -0.013246818445622921, -0.039031997323036194, -0.0016717257676646113, 0.0026316524017602205, 0.002081929473206401, 0.0032699324656277895, -0.0070110559463500